RussianDocs OCR — third-party components and the scope of the licence
=====================================================================

This file exists because `LICENSE` cannot answer two questions on its own: what the
MIT grant covers besides source code, and what in this repository is somebody else's
work under other terms. Nothing here modifies `LICENSE`; adding conditions inside
the MIT text would stop it from being MIT.


1. WHAT THE MIT LICENCE COVERS
------------------------------

The MIT licence in `LICENSE` covers BOTH:

  * the source code — `document_processing/`, `service/`, `web/`, `ports/`,
    `conformance/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`;

  * the TRAINED MODEL WEIGHTS shipped with it — everything under
    `document_processing/models/`, which is about 215 MB: the `.onnx` files, the
    `model.json` configuration beside each of them, and `centers.npz`.

The second point is stated explicitly because weights are not code and a licence on
a repository is not automatically a licence on the artefacts inside it. A reader who
wants to use this in a product needs the answer, and the answer is: **the weights are
under the same MIT terms as the code** — use, modify, redistribute, including
commercially, with the copyright notice preserved.

Note what this does NOT claim: nothing is said here about the datasets the models were
trained on. Those are not distributed with this repository, and no rights to them are
granted or implied.


2. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS INCLUDED IN THIS REPOSITORY
-----------------------------------------------------

Fonts, in `web/public/fonts/` — self-hosted so that a deployment beside a GPU with no
outbound internet renders the interface it was tested with, rather than silently
falling back to a system font:

  * Inter — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Copyright (c) 2016 The Inter Project Authors
    https://github.com/rsms/inter
    Licence text: `web/public/fonts/LICENSE-Inter.txt`

  * JetBrains Mono — SIL Open Font License 1.1
    Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors
    https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono
    Licence text: `web/public/fonts/LICENSE-JetBrainsMono.txt`

Both licence files are copied VERBATIM from each project's own upstream licence file, which is what the
OFL requires: clause 2 says every copy of the font software must carry the copyright notice and this
licence. Each font's file contains its own copyright line, so they are kept separate rather than merged —
merging them would mean deciding which notice belongs to which file, and getting that wrong is exactly
the failure the clause exists to prevent.

No other third-party source, binary or asset is vendored here. Runtime dependencies
are declared in `requirements2026.txt`, `requirements-service.txt`, `web/package.json`
and each port's manifest, and are fetched from their own repositories under their own
terms — they are not redistributed by this project.

Previously vendored and REMOVED (2026-08-07): a set of proprietary .NET assemblies
under `document_processing/ctc/OcrLib462_2024/`, imported by nothing and incompatible
with an MIT distribution. They remain in earlier commits; see
`docs/merge-ports-to-main.md` for the history rewrite that is planned before the
public merge.


